PSQL Commands:

- To enable UTF-8 encoding for terminal run:
chcp 65001

- To enter the database run:
psql {External Database URL}

- To enable PostgreSQL table to display UTF-8 characters run:
\encoding UTF-8

\dt - list all tables
\d {table name} - show table details

SELECT * FROM {table name}

- The External Database URL is in your database provider's dashboard.
  Keep it in the DATABASE_URL environment variable; never commit it. Example:
psql "$DATABASE_URL"

Database:

- The schema lives in db/schema.sql. The server never creates or changes tables;
  at startup it only logs DB_SCHEMA_MISSING_TABLES if some are missing.
- New empty database:
psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f db/schema.sql

- Main tables: users (everyone who logs in, with a role), students (profile of a
  student user), faculties / degrees / programs (lookup lists), courses (called
  "classes" in the API), course_enrollments, lessons (one per attendance session),
  attendance_records (one row per student per lesson) and attendance_statuses.
  Lesson and attendance counts are not stored; the student_course_attendance view
  counts them.
- New attendance status (e.g. late): insert a row into attendance_statuses.
  New faculty or specialization: insert rows into faculties / programs.
- db/migrate_from_legacy.sql converted the old tables (teachers, classes,
  class_students, attendances, attendance_timestamps) into this schema; the steps
  are at the top of that file.
